# ControlRig Stable Authoring Phase 1 Handoff

Date: 2026-06-30

Scope: Phase 1 read-only skeleton profile and recipe-planning evidence for the
ControlRig stable authoring plan. This report is source/tooling evidence only.
It does not record any original asset mutation, runtime/gameplay module change,
solver unit expansion, or binding-contract promotion.

## Ieta Review Line

- Keep original Unreal assets read-only.
- Keep writes limited to `/Game/_MCP_Temp` or `/Game/_MCP_Sample` for later live
  smokes.
- Do not add runtime/gameplay modules.
- Do not expand solver units in this phase.
- Do not add a static C++ dependency from `UnrealMCP` to
  `UnrealMCPControlRigToolsEditor`.
- Do not use generic Python reflection to probe protected ControlRig, RigVM, or
  AnimGraph internals.
- Do not serialize MCP-only references into generated assets.

## Tivret Implementation Evidence

- `profile_controlrig_skeleton` is the Phase 1 read-only MCP-facing route.
- `UUnrealMCPControlRigAuthoringSubsystem::ProfileSkeletonJson` reads bounded
  skeleton or skeletal mesh profile data without creating, compiling, saving,
  executing, or solving assets.
- The Python wrapper adds recipe-planning evidence:
  - bounded bone list and parent chains;
  - candidate humanoid aliases;
  - missing or ambiguous alias names;
  - controls-only preset recommendations.
- The planning evidence remains analysis data. It does not author a recipe,
  mutate an asset, or add solver units.

